\f0\fs36 \cf0 Got the atari 800 DOS working upstairs. The BASIC is kind of nice.\
\
Been reading "Atari Basic Programs in Minutes" that has a pretty slick method of storing subroutines on disk (distinct from the programs that use them) - and then loading them and chaining the real program.\
It's also a nice set of subroutines, and needs some digging in to.\
\
I haven't seen how they do it yet, but they have a A1$="" : A2$ = "" ... : A8$ = "", and are able to use a subset of those based on a numeric variable (so programaticlly it's constructing "A1$" vs "A2$" and then accessing that variable.\
This book also has a disk-based "database" that merits some looking in to.\
\
It has a TRAP call for handling things, like EOF\
\
To start DOS, turn on the machine with a DOS disk.  BASIC then has file I/O.  Use DOS for a menu-based interface for copying disks, getting directory listings, etc.\
